; Vendored err_trace (see README.md). `upstream/` is a git submodule, i.e. a
; whole upstream repository checked out inside this tree - not the two source
; files we actually build. Its own dune files (test/dune, bench/dune) declare a
; test suite depending on ppx_expect, base, time_now and compiler-libs.
;
; The enclosing asm/dune marks this tree `vendored_dirs`, which suppresses
; warnings and leaves it out of `@fmt`, but that alone does not stop dune
; reading `upstream/`'s own dune files: left visible, those stanzas land in
; `dune describe` output, and tools/asm_audit.ml classifies anything under
; vendor/ as part of the production closure (see its `production_dirs`). base,
; time_now and ppx_expect are all on its `denied` list, so `make asm-purity`
; fails - and on a CI image that does not ship ppx_expect, `dune build @all`
; fails outright.
;
; `data_only_dirs` is what stops that: dune keeps upstream/'s files as ordinary
; sources - the copy_files# below still reaches them - but reads no dune file
; inside it.
;
; tools/asm-check-planted.sh has a case that deletes this line and requires the
; purity audit to reject the result, so the protection cannot be lost silently.
(data_only_dirs upstream)

; `wrapped false` is upstream's own setting and is load-bearing: it is what
; makes the module `Err` rather than `Err_trace.Err`, which is the name the
; whole codebase uses.
;
; Melange mode lives in melange/vendor/err_trace, and the nested tool project's
; own copy lives in tools/vendor/err_trace, both of which copy_files these same
; sources; a dune project boundary cannot share a library, and dune cannot make
; `modes` conditional within one stanza either.

(copy_files#
 (files upstream/src/err.ml))

(copy_files#
 (files upstream/src/err.mli))

(library
 (name err_trace)
 (wrapped false)
 (modes byte native)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{env:ASM_MELANGE=false} true)))
